{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/570434-2e-forsaken-vs-pures-ratio","id":570434,"title":"2E Forsaken vs Pures ratio","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-27T12:36:22-07:00","id":570434,"title":"2E Forsaken vs Pures ratio","content":"Hi everyone, I will soon launch a long game with Werewolf, and the Pures will be among the main protaganist. Also, I still have in my head the first ed ratio that Pures largely outnumbered Forsaken. But after reading the 2ed book I don't remember any allusion to such thing. So is the many to one ratio between Pures and Forsaken still a canon thing or not ?<br /> <br /> (I know, as a GM I can do as I want, but still an official answer would be nice ^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:04:44-07:00","id":570468,"title":"","content":"The official answer is that the ratio is what ever it needs to be to suit your story. There's no canonical numbers, it's very intentionally left vague so you can pick what ever ratio you want and it won't contradict official material. I don't say that to shut your question down, just to stress that there's really no right answer to be found. Though, it's still fun to kick ideas around.<br /> <br /> All that said, the 1e assumption that the pure outnumber the forsaken does still work just fine if you want a baseline to draw from. It's what I still use in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-27-2015, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T20:03:26-07:00","id":570843,"title":"","content":"Well, on a global level it doesn't really matter, werewolves function on a local level.<br /> <br /> So wherever you're gaming, what makes sense? Unless things change in second edition, the pure are less urban, what with their anti-human sentiments and one of their tribes being luddites, so in downtown New York? Probably more forsaken. The bayou? Probably significantly more pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:12:55-07:00","id":570875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/570434-2e-forsaken-vs-pures-ratio?p=570843#post570843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, on a global level it doesn't really matter, werewolves function on a local level.<br /> <br /> So wherever you're gaming, what makes sense? Unless things change in second edition, the pure are less urban, what with their anti-human sentiments and one of their tribes being luddites, so in downtown New York? Probably more forsaken. The bayou? Probably significantly more pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Ivory Claws are fairly urbanized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:52:09-07:00","id":570908,"title":"","content":"The Fire-Touched seemed to have changed to have more of a presence in the Shadow, which may mean in both urban and rural areas.<br /> <br /> But like Charlaquin said, the only concrete numbers are the ones you want to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:58:06-07:00","id":571148,"title":"","content":"The numbers really depend on where you are, too. Fire Touched would likely have a far weaker hold in areas where religion in general is weak, ivory in areas of less racial segregation, and naturally, we have an entire Tribe that can't handle living in cities. <br /> <br /> A lot of this is going to reflect the general attitude you grew up with, pre-Change. If the local culture doesn't lend itself to the uncompromising mindsets of the Pure, then actually having them be a majority is difficult to imagine.<br /> <br /> Sadly, that mindset is far from uncommon in reality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T16:55:33-07:00","id":573318,"title":"","content":"According to the first Ed canon and the book blood of the wolf, as well as other books, here are some numbers to go on.<br /> <br /> If you assume under half a million uratha around the world, with about 35% being forsaken, you have about 300,000 pure facing off against 180,000 forsaken.<br /> <br /> In the wilderness and rural areas, the Pure dominate, and the Predator kings are howling for blood. The Pure are about double the Forsaken, if not more. If you want a better idea of a territory dominated by the pure, read about Santa Fe in the book, The Pure. That would be a microcosm of the state of the world where the Pure Dominate (ie. Most places). Read shadows of the UK to see where the Pure are numerically outnumbered, but still dominate the Forsaken. In these areas all bets are off and battles are ugly and brutal and Basu lim happens a lot because there are no humans to witness.<br /> <br /> In cities, there are more Forsaken because the Pure hate cities. At best the Pure may be at parity. However, cities are filled with humans, vampires, prometheans, mages, you name it. Shifting into The war form is risky unless you want to attract a CNN news crew. Battles are in the shadows and you are more likely to face subtle Ivory Claws pulling the strings. Werewolves must make more effort to be hidden lest the herd get spooked. The Pure may be more likely to partner with Hosts and Claimed in cities to hunt Forsaken, as well as human allies.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:29:06-07:00","id":573387,"title":"","content":"Considering that the Detroit write-up in 2E has the Predator Kings dominant, you can even play around with that. It's as much of a hunting ground as any other, and clearly they're making a mess over there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}